{
  "schemaVersion": 3,
  "id": "night-road",
  "name": "Night Road",
  "tagline": "Tyres on a night road, an engine's low purr, a running acid line.",
  "description": "The low rush of tyres on a night road and an engine's purr; the air moves with the acid line's slow sweep. A steady four-four, a bass rolling into each beat, sixteenth ticks, a single-note acid line under long sweeps, a warm pad underneath.",
  "use": {
    "name": "Sprint",
    "for": "Short, timeboxed bursts: first drafts, fast output.",
    "why": "The fastest tempo, for forward momentum, but it hits no harder than the rest: the drive comes from a bass rolling into each beat and the road moving with the music. The research puts the useful energising range at about 115–125 bpm and finds that faster can tip over, so Sprint sits just above it and is for short blocks, not whole sessions. It builds fastest."
  },
